# Hand-written OWL axioms the reasoner layers on top of the generated TBox (bbqs.owl.ttl).
#
# WHY HAND-WRITTEN: gen-owl drops LinkML `disjoint_with` (Phase 4 finding), and "every node class is
# disjoint from every other" is not expressible in LinkML without an N×N `disjoint_with` list. So this
# file is the OWL twin of shapes/consistency.shapes.ttl: the contradiction axioms a generator can't
# produce. tests/guards/kg-owl-disjointness.test.mjs keeps it honest against the schema and exporter.
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix bbqs: <https://brain-bbqs.org/schema#> .

# Mirrors `disjoint_with` in bbqs.linkml.yaml (Person <-> Organization), which gen-owl did not emit.
bbqs:Person owl:disjointWith bbqs:Organization .

# Invariants #1 and #3: one node = one resource_type = one class. Every concrete node class is
# pairwise disjoint from every other, so a node typed Investigator AND Project -- or a held_by that
# points at a Project, making it an inferred Investigator -- is a logical contradiction.
#
# Deliberately NOT listed: subclasses of a listed class (Benchmark, Dandiset are Datasets -- listing
# them would make them unsatisfiable), the abstract schema.org anchors, and the enum classes.
[] a owl:AllDisjointClasses ;
  owl:members (
    bbqs:Investigator
    bbqs:ResearchOrganization
    bbqs:Consortium
    bbqs:FundingAgency
    bbqs:DeviceManufacturer
    bbqs:WorkingGroup
    bbqs:Project
    bbqs:ProjectRole
    bbqs:Publication
    bbqs:Dataset
    bbqs:SoftwareTool
    bbqs:Tool
    bbqs:Algorithm
    bbqs:MLModel
    bbqs:Protocol
    bbqs:Announcement
    bbqs:Job
    bbqs:FundingOpportunity
    bbqs:Event
    bbqs:Species
    bbqs:Device
    bbqs:DeviceCategory
    bbqs:ExperimentalData
    bbqs:MarrModel
    bbqs:ProvenanceRecord
    bbqs:SourceClass
  ) .
